From 54571b39d25346901896b77425ddab68436a30ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roy Shih <royshih.cs11@nycu.edu.tw>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 03:15:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] turbomind: w4a16 for sm_120

Registers the mma.m16n8k16 w4a16 kernels under an Sm120 tag. They were already
being compiled for sm_120a; a half-open arch range (Sm80 = Arch<800,900>) made
Registry::Add reject them host-side and compiled every body away device-side,
so this card registered zero quantized GEMMs -- only the cuBLAS fallback.

- kernel/sm120_16816_4.cu: 55 sm80 tiles re-tagged Sm120, plus dense and
  grouped bf16 blocks (Qwen3.5-27B is bf16; upstream forces fp16 for AWQ).
- arch/config_sm80_s16816.h: Config_U4_d takes Operand_A<T>/Tc = T rather than
  hardcoded half, so the *dense* w4a16 path can serve bf16. No-op for the
  T = half instantiations every other arch uses.
- core/common.h + iterator_sm80.h: TURBOMIND_ARCH_HAS_L2_EVICT_POLICY. sm_12x
  faults with an illegal instruction when the cp.async L2 evict-first hint is
  applied to the packed-B operand. The hint is performance-only, so dropping
  it there cannot change results.
- core/mma.h: include <cuda_bf16.h>. CUDA 13 stopped pulling it in
  transitively, breaking every sm70/75/80 kernel TU, not just this one.

Verified on RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell: 2 -> 222 registered kernels, 28/28 numerics
against a dequant reference, 2.3-3.3x on decode GEMMs.
